message: "If you use ENTITY in research, engineering, evaluation, or derivative work, please cite this software release."
title: "ENTITY: Sovereign Digital Authority, Provenance, Data Rights, Recovery and BTDU"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Blackmore
    given-names: Shawn
    affiliation: "Blackmore Technology Group Limited"
version: 3.4.2
date-released: 2026-09-26
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/blackmore-technology-group/ENTITY"
url: "https://blackmore-technology-group.github.io/ENTITY-DOCS/"
abstract: >-
  ENTITY is an open protocol and reference implementation for persistent digital
  identity, delegated authority, provenance and evidence, rights, portable
  recovery, and interoperable economic state. ENTITY v3.4.2 introduces the
  Blackmore Technology Data Universe (BTDU), an ENTITY-governed atom/bond
  information substrate that preserves protocol authority, rights, provenance,
  recovery, and economic boundaries.
keywords:
  - digital identity
  - data provenance
  - data governance
  - data rights
  - sovereign data
  - knowledge graph
  - AI governance
  - interoperability
  - open protocol
  - BTDU
